{:edb/db-before-t 1859 :edb/db-after-t 1860 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535172 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:38:19.361Z" 13194139535172 true] [17592186087504 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/bfdf3147fb8488c3a0032f9dad326b5d8c3ff68be46738dc39215e5098af6272.png)\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b?$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186087504 1100 "$\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b$?" 13194139535172 false] [17592186087504 1145 "Given the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/35814ac6d965ac688907d162b45d9b0b194ea40375d4e474466e4fb4b1de1c1b.png) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8x-5y \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ -4x+5y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5y-8x \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ 5y-4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/f59824c26875665fcbd8adfc5414fa7b0c60254e01f725f9ca72cf1d370a3e8b.png)\n\nFinally, $a-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1.$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186087504 1145 "Given the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-8x - 5y \\\\ -3x - 6y \\\\ -4x + 5y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-5y - 8x \\\\ -3x - 6y \\\\ 5y - 4x\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1\n$$" 13194139535172 false] [17592186087505 1100 "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$, find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$.\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535172 false] [17592186087505 1100 "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/7a6d4db6774da29f9b89996e348fad61b281737db6b44e9a39efa016fa2f15f3.png)" 13194139535172 true] [17592186087505 1145 "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(v) &= T \\cdot v \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535172 false] [17592186087505 1145 "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186087519 1100 "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/81d01f5d724e8b9d186bc53a15b488868c5c2d5d661f09d7c1febd862011afba.png)" 13194139535172 true] [17592186087519 1100 "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535172 false] [17592186087519 1145 "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/412113c303aa31d5a9c23d5b0fa45201a8803b96f5239b9b1d007fc5128413c9.png)\n\nNotice that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/bcd58c5310e4312fdbcc5619e0a89a03afb9bd5a6adff9a851e34d19e2bafb0b.png)\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/67da7147fc2e767f6c1fe15d2664d7f0b0e5f7b0778b168c6f702d2b999a2799.png)" 13194139535172 true] [17592186087519 1145 "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNotice that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535172 false] [17592186087690 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335395 13194139535172 true] [17592186087690 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335437 13194139535172 true] [17592186087690 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335444 13194139535172 true] [17592186087691 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335402 13194139535172 true] [17592186087691 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335409 13194139535172 true] [17592186087691 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335451 13194139535172 true] [17592186087691 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335458 13194139535172 true] [17592186087701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335416 13194139535172 true] [17592186087701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335423 13194139535172 true] [17592186087701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335430 13194139535172 true] [17592186088102 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535172 true] [17592186088102 1100 "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T: R^{2} → R^{3}$, find $T(v)$.\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}, v = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535172 false] [17592186088102 1100 "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088102 1145 "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088103 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535172 true] [17592186088103 1100 "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}ay+2x-2z \\\\ bz-3x+cy\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088103 1100 "$T = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}ay + 2x - 2z \\\\ bz - 3x + cy\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T: R^{3} → R^{2}$ shown above. What is the value of $a + b + c$?" 13194139535172 false] [17592186088103 1145 "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-3y-2z \\\\ -3x-y+4z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3y+2x-2z \\\\ 4z-3x-y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3y+2x-2z \\\\ 4z-3x+(-1)y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=4+(-3)+(-1)=0.$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088104 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535172 true] [17592186088104 1100 "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ ax-8y \\\\ -9x+by\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b?$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088104 1100 "$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}, T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-3x + y \\\\ ax - 8y \\\\ -9x + by\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T: R^{2} → R^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a + b$?" 13194139535172 false] [17592186088104 1145 "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b=-2+7=5.$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088324 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535172 true] [17592186088324 1100 "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088324 1100 "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $T: R^{3} → R^{2}$, where\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2x - y + z \\\\ x - y - z\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535172 false] [17592186088324 1145 "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x+(-1)y+1z \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+(-1)z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088326 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535172 true] [17592186088326 1100 "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x-3y+8z \\\\ x+z+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186088326 1100 "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $T: R^{3} → R^{2}$, where\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x - 3y + 8z \\\\ x + z + 2y\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535172 false] [17592186088326 1145 "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1x+(-3)y+8z \\\\ 1x+2y+1z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x-3y+8z \\\\ x+z+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335395 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335396 13194139535172 true] [17592186335395 1089 "q-140422" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335395 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535172 true] [17592186335395 1100 "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+bx \\\\ -6x+cy\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $c+b?$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335395 1113 #uuid "f6c6739f-0bc4-58a0-97c1-be61353fa33d" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335395 1145 "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ -x+3y \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y-x \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+(-1)x \\\\ -6x+(7)y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $c+b=(-1)+7=6.$" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335397 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335398 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335399 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335400 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335401 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1041 "selection" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335399 13194139535172 true] [17592186335396 1110 #uuid "f53b953b-0e7f-5c57-83d2-d0e5010d5d34" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335397 1034 "8" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535172 true] [17592186335397 1111 #uuid "705bb233-0253-59bf-a5c2-fa2874395dee" 13194139535172 true] [17592186335398 1034 "2" 13194139535172 true]